import json,statistics as st,random,sys,html
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(sys.argv[1]); rows=[json.loads(x) for x in (p/'games.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
mean=lambda xs:round(st.mean(xs),2) if xs else None
summary=[]
for copies in [4,9]:
 for players in [None,2,3,4]:
  for version in ['133-finite-dice-preview','135-activation-dice-preview']:
   r=[x for x in rows if x['copies']==copies and (players is None or x['players']==players) and x['version']==version]; f=[x for x in r if x.get('endReason')=='finish']; done=[x for x in r if x['status']=='complete']; gaps=sorted(x['range'] for x in f)
   summary.append(dict(copies=copies,players=players or 'all',version=version[:3],n=len(r),finished=len(f),exhausted=sum(x.get('endReason')=='deckExhausted' for x in r),failed=sum(x['status']=='failed' for x in r),censored=sum(x['status']=='censored' for x in r),gap=mean([x['range'] for x in f]),third=mean([x['thirdLag'] for x in f]),zero=mean([x['zero'] for x in f]),actions=mean([x['actions'] for x in done]),finishActions=mean([x['actions'] for x in f]),gapMedian=st.median(gaps) if gaps else None,gapP90=gaps[min(len(gaps)-1,int(.9*len(gaps)))] if gaps else None))
paired=[];rng=random.Random(135)
for copies in [4,9]:
 pairs=[]
 for a in rows:
  if a['copies']!=copies or not a['version'].startswith('133'):continue
  b=next(x for x in rows if x['copies']==copies and x['seed']==a['seed'] and x['players']==a['players'] and x['cohort']==a['cohort'] and x['version'].startswith('135'))
  pairs.append((a,b))
 for metric in ['finish','range','thirdLag']:
  valid=pairs if metric=='finish' else [(a,b) for a,b in pairs if a.get('endReason')==b.get('endReason')=='finish']
  strata={}
  for a,b in valid:
   delta=int(b.get('endReason')=='finish')-int(a.get('endReason')=='finish') if metric=='finish' else b[metric]-a[metric]
   strata.setdefault((a['players'],a['cohort']),[]).append(delta)
  draws=sorted(st.mean([rng.choice(v) for v in strata.values() for _ in v]) for _ in range(4000)) if valid else []
  paired.append(dict(copies=copies,metric=metric,n=len(valid),delta=mean([x for v in strata.values() for x in v]),ci95=[round(draws[int(len(draws)*q)],3) for q in [.025,.975]] if draws else []))
(p/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(summary=summary,paired=paired),indent=2))
print(json.dumps(dict(summary=summary,paired=paired),indent=2))
manifest=json.loads((p/'manifest.json').read_text()); reviews=json.loads((p/'sample-review.json').read_text())
def table(rs,keys):
 return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+html.escape(k)+'</th>' for k in keys)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(r.get(k,'—')))+'</td>' for k in keys)+'</tr>' for r in rs)+'</tbody></table>'
body='''<h1>The timing fix did not make the simulated race tighter</h1><p>v135 own-company activation · timing-01 · 8 November 2026</p><p>240 matched-setup games across old/new timing, four/nine cards per company, 2–4 players, balanced self-play and mixed policies. Ten additional corrected games have full reviewed traces and verified replays. No game rules were changed for this study.</p><h2>Nine cards per company: a viable finish, still a wide race</h2><p>Among games reaching 24, the mean first–last gap was <b>22.47 before → 22.60 after</b>; first–third was <b>15.98 → 16.35</b>. Completion was 59/60 → 57/60. On the 56 matched pairs where both finished, the gap changed +0.12 spaces, bootstrap 95% interval −0.27 to +0.52. There is no clear improvement. About four companies still paid $0 at exit.</p>'''
body+=table([r for r in summary if r['players']=='all' and r['copies']==9],['version','n','finished','gap','third','zero','actions','finishActions','gapMedian','gapP90'])
body+='''<h2>The live four-card deck is still insufficient</h2><p>The browser default is still four cards/company, not the nine-card diagnostic. Corrected timing finished only 12/60 games at24; 48 exhausted all cards. At four players it finished just1/20. Early exhaustion is not counted as a spread success. The former four-card balance recommendation remains withdrawn.</p><h2>What remains behind the spread?</h2><ol><li><b>Bot decision-making is a material confounder.</b> In sample8207, a player with $20, no shares in the leading company, and alternative cards funded that company at22. Its opponent won the auction and the game,119–20. The funding heuristic ranks expected exit price plus relative holdings; it does not explicitly evaluate terminal score or the chance of winning the auction. This behavior can sustain concentrated investment despite strategic reasons to withhold a card.</li><li><b>Some companies receive no investment.</b> In sample8208, C0 and C5 received every fundraising action; four companies remained on1 or3. Scarcity redirected attention between two contenders, not across the whole field. The game ended when the first company reached24.</li><li><b>Explicit reactions and value effects still bypass matching-card movement.</b> This is intended: Aidan advanced the eventual winner on fumbles in8206; Danilo followed movement in8209; value cards moved leaders in8205 and8210. Gill's old global timing is no longer needed to produce wide gaps.</li></ol><p><b>Next discriminating test:</b> correct the bots' auction/terminal-score awareness while holding rules fixed, then repeat the comparison. Do not tune company-card quantities around clearly self-defeating offers. Draw-two and card-free support actions have not yet been retested with corrected timing.</p>'''
body+='<details><summary>Player counts, policies and uncertainty</summary><p>Gaps and zero-payout counts use only finish-at24 games; action means use all completed games. There are20 games per version/supply/player-count cell; ten in each policy cohort. These are small diagnostic cohorts, not proof of human balance. Provisional targets: ≥95% finish, first–last mean≤16, first–third≤8. Nine-card corrected completion meets the point threshold, but both spread targets fail and completion uncertainty is substantial. Four-card completion fails.</p>'
body+=table(summary,['copies','players','version','n','finished','exhausted','gap','third','zero','actions','failed','censored'])
coh=[]
for copies in [4,9]:
 for version in ['133','135']:
  for cohort in ['self','mixed']:
   r=[x for x in rows if x['copies']==copies and x['version'].startswith(version) and x['cohort']==cohort];f=[x for x in r if x.get('endReason')=='finish'];coh.append(dict(copies=copies,version=version,cohort=cohort,n=len(r),finished=len(f),gap=mean([x['range'] for x in f])))
body+=table(coh,['copies','version','cohort','n','finished','gap'])+table(paired,['copies','metric','n','delta','ci95'])+'<p>Delta=new−old. Finish deltas are proportions. Paired spread comparisons condition on both versions reaching24; they are not identical to differences between the two unconditional finish cohorts. Bootstrap resamples complete matched game pairs within player-count/cohort strata,4,000 draws. With only six eligible four-card pairs, its narrow interval is not useful general evidence. Same seeds do not preserve subsequent rolls after decisions diverge. Forecast changes accompany the timing fix; other decision logic is unchanged. No claim of optimal play or tabletop minutes.</p></details>'
body+='<h2>Ten complete game reviews</h2><p>All fixed sample slots completed; none replaced. Five four-card exhaustion games and five nine-card finish games are retained as selected. C0–C5 denote company IDs. E numbers are zero-based event indices in the linked full trace. Decision snapshots contain only information available to the acting bot, plus public state.</p>'
for review in reviews:
 seed=review['seed'];g=json.loads((p/f'samples/{seed}.json').read_text());events=g['events'];
 body+=f'<details><summary>Game {seed} · {g["meta"]["players"]} players · {g["meta"]["copies"]} cards/company · {g["meta"]["endReason"]}</summary><p>{html.escape(review["review"])}</p><p><a href="samples/{seed}.json">Full trace and dice evaluations</a> · <a href="samples/{seed}-replay.json">Importable replay</a> · <a href="samples/{seed}-actions.json">Every action: hand, holdings, cash and market</a></p><details><summary>Complete ordered event trace</summary>'
 body+='<table><tr><th>Event</th><th>Type</th><th>Data</th></tr>'+''.join(f'<tr id="game-{seed}-e{i}"><td>E{i}</td><td>{html.escape(e["type"])}</td><td><code>{html.escape(json.dumps(e,ensure_ascii=False))}</code></td></tr>' for i,e in enumerate(events))+'</table></details></details>'
body+=f'<details><summary>Reproduction, source identity and checks</summary><p>Source SHA256: <code>{manifest["source"]}</code>. All240 primary games completed: zero failed/censored. All ten full sample command streams replayed to identical logs and scores, including settlement. Interactive production dice forecasts were used. Event traces expose intended founder reactions, not purely additive causal attribution; founderMovement totals are diagnostic only.</p><p><a href="manifest.json">Frozen protocol</a> · <a href="games.jsonl">240 raw results</a> · <a href="metrics.json">Metrics</a> · <a href="runtime.json">Runtime</a> · <a href="source/scripts/activation-timing-study.js">Frozen runner</a> · <a href="source/scripts/activation-timing-report.py">Report generator</a></p><pre>node scripts/activation-timing-study.js NEW_DIRECTORY\npython3 scripts/activation-timing-report.py NEW_DIRECTORY</pre><p>The report generator also requires the authored sample-review.json. Old/new source trees and dependency lockfile are preserved under source/. No rules or bot code was edited during or after the cohort.</p></details>'
(p/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>v135 timing comparison</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1c2925;background:#f8f6ef;max-width:1080px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:36px}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;max-width:100%;display:block;overflow:auto;margin:18px 0}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;text-align:left}th{background:#e4eadb}details{margin:18px 0;padding:16px;background:white;border:1px solid #d1d8cf;border-radius:8px}summary{font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;white-space:pre-wrap}a{color:#145e48}li{margin:14px 0}</style>'+body+'</html>')
